`bmb check` does not report the diagnostic E0263 yet: a closure's parameters and result have their types written (ADR-0053 §2). It came with the commit "Closures without captures (ADR-0053, 2V-20b)". Implement it. Examples of what `bmb check` must print (one JSON line per diagnostic; the path in `file` is the one given on the command line), each after the source line it points at:

    apply::<_>(|x| -> i64 { x }, 1)
    {"code": "E0263", "severity": "error", "message": "closure parameter `x` needs its type", "file": "err/fn_values.bmb", "line": 29, "col": 21, "end_line": 29, "end_col": 22, "fix": {"message": "write `x: T` (types are written, DESIGN §4.1)"}}

    let add = |y: i64| y + 1;
    {"code": "E0263", "severity": "error", "message": "a closure needs its result type", "file": "err/rust_paths.bmb", "line": 20, "col": 19, "end_line": 20, "end_col": 27, "fix": {"message": "write `-> T` or `-> (r: T)` after the parameters"}}

Everything else the program prints must stay as it is.

